Your Blog Will Outlive Your Database (It Doesn&amp;#39;t Have To)</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-24-your-blog-will-outlive-your-database/</link><pubDate>Fri, 24 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-24-your-blog-will-outlive-your-database/</guid><description>Your reader&amp;#39;s words evaporate while your writer&amp;#39;s words endure. Markdown won the durability war by being boring. Every time we add interactivity, we drag back the database, and durability dies. There&amp;#39;s a missing primitive: writes that are as durable as the reads. Git is that primitive.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2026-04-24-your-blog-will-outlive-your-database/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Local-First</media:title></media:content><category>git-native-publishing</category><category>commit-as-write</category><category>local-first</category><category>static-sites</category><category>durability</category><category>jamstack</category></item></channel></rss>